(Clatter)

491
00:19:23,265 --> 00:19:24,667
I just lost a shoe.

492
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,874
Well, how did we do, Miss Heck?

493
00:19:37,994 --> 00:19:39,327
I guess you'll tell <i>me.</i>

494
00:19:39,507 --> 00:19:42,253
Class, while I grade
all your fine work,

495
00:19:42,385 --> 00:19:44,821
you can continue reading
chapter 23.

496
00:19:45,071 --> 00:19:48,933
If you finish, you can proceed
to chapter 24. (Pen clicks)

497
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:51,254
<i>(Sue) Is smiling contagious?</i>

498
00:19:51,364 --> 00:19:53,715
<i>After many attempts</i>
<i>with multiple subjects,</i>

499
00:19:53,842 --> 00:19:57,094
<i>including family, friends,</i>
<i>a Red Lobster waitress,</i>

500
00:19:57,210 --> 00:19:58,678
<i>and an unfriendly baby,</i>

501
00:19:58,896 --> 00:20:03,983
<i>I, unfortunately, was unable</i>
<i>to prove my hypothesis.</i>

502
00:20:04,099 --> 00:20:06,575
<i>However, like many scientists</i>
<i>before me,</i>

503
00:20:06,709 --> 00:20:08,694
<i>I refuse to admit defeat.</i>

504
00:20:08,799 --> 00:20:13,044
<i>It took Einstein ten years</i>
<i>to prove E=mc2,</i>

505
00:20:13,161 --> 00:20:16,263
<i>and if it takes me that long</i>
<i>to prove smiling is contagious,</i>

506
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:18,354
<i>then I am up for the challenge,</i>

507
00:20:18,469 --> 00:20:21,854
<i>for I believe there are</i>
<i>some things that defy logic.</i>

508
00:20:21,961 --> 00:20:23,612
No way! An iPad?!

509
00:20:23,789 --> 00:20:25,213
And it's the one from the fire?

510
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:29,419
(Laughs) Oh, this is better
than being a good parent.

511
00:20:30,369 --> 00:20:32,543
<i>French anatomist Duchenne</i>
<i>wrote that</i>

512
00:20:32,661 --> 00:20:35,706
<i>"Joy is expressed on the face</i>
<i>by contraction of the muscles,</i>

513
00:20:35,836 --> 00:20:38,530
<i>but it can only be put in play</i>

514
00:20:38,657 --> 00:20:41,194
<i>by the sweet emotions</i>
<i>of the soul."</i>

515
00:20:41,292 --> 00:20:42,566
Gonna miss you guys.

516
00:20:42,915 --> 00:20:44,611
Okay. I'm just
gonna say it.

517
00:20:45,064 --> 00:20:46,437
I love you.

518
00:20:46,549 --> 00:20:48,958
- Oh. Oh, I--
- Okay, Darrin just made it weird.

519
00:20:49,066 --> 00:20:51,633
I'm sorry. (Voice breaking)
I'm very emotional right now.

520
00:20:51,746 --> 00:20:53,916
Yeah. Dude, come on, man.
(Laughs)

521
00:20:54,087 --> 00:20:57,226
<i>And Duchenne had a whole smile</i>
<i>named after him.</i>

522
00:20:57,328 --> 00:20:58,703
<i>Think of the smiles</i>
<i>over the years</i>

523
00:20:58,817 --> 00:21:01,573
<i>that have inspired</i>
<i>a whole world to happiness--</i>

524
00:21:01,678 --> 00:21:04,593
<i>Mona Lisa's, Justin Bieber's.</i>

525
00:21:04,709 --> 00:21:06,438
<i>Some might laugh at me, I know,</i>

526
00:21:06,546 --> 00:21:08,507
<i>just as they laughed</i>
<i>at John Gurdon.</i>

527
00:21:08,629 --> 00:21:11,832
<i>He was told in high school that</i>
<i>he would never be a scientist.</i>

528
00:21:11,982 --> 00:21:14,576
<i>He just won the Nobel prize.</i>

529
00:21:14,706 --> 00:21:17,633
<i>I guess it just proves that</i>
<i>being dismissed by people</i>

530
00:21:17,754 --> 00:21:19,117
<i>who think they know better</i>

531
00:21:19,225 --> 00:21:22,744
<i>is not an obstacle to winning</i>
<i>a Nobel prize.</i>

532
00:21:22,897 --> 00:21:25,439
<i>So I will continue</i>
<i>with my research--</i>

533
00:21:25,553 --> 00:21:27,350
<i>one smile at a time,</i>

534
00:21:27,464 --> 00:21:31,528
<i>until I prove</i>
<i>that smiling</i> is <i>contagious,</i>

535
00:21:31,653 --> 00:21:35,339
<i>'cause I don't wanna live</i>
<i>in a world where it isn't.</i>

536
00:21:39,617 --> 00:21:43,927
Sync and corrections by n17t01
